==============================================================================
ROOT CAUSE
==============================================================================
  • Toolchain drift: the runner has Swift 6.3.2 but the repo's locked baseline (ADR-012,
    apps/apple/versions.lock.md) is Swift 6.0.1. Under 6.3.2, a widespread pre-existing pattern
    fails to compile: a `private func glass(@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View)` helper
    (non-escaping) whose `content` is passed into `TSGlassPanel { content()... }` (whose
    initializer parameter is `@escaping`). Capturing a non-escaping parameter in an escaping
    closure is rejected.
        $ grep -rl "@ViewBuilder _ content: () -> some View" apps/apple --include=*.swift | wc -l
        42      ← 42 out-of-scope sibling files carry this exact pattern.
  • macOS additionally requires a development signing certificate the runner does not have.
  • Both blockers are in files / environment OUTSIDE this prompt's allowed files
    (apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/OnboardingWizard.*, the log). Fixing 42 sibling
    surfaces or provisioning signing would violate the allowed-files scope and the
    no-cross-scope / no-delegation rules, and would collide with the prompts that own those files.

